\[\frac{1}{\cos x} - \frac{1}{\sin x} = \frac{\sin x - \cos x}{\sin x \cos x}.\]Since both sides have the same denominator, we can multiply both sides by $\sin x \cos x$ to obtain $\sin^6 x \cos^6 x = \sin x - \cos x.$

On the left-hand side, we apply AM-GM:
